# F1. Java semantics for int/long division, which Wasm lacks (x / 0 traps; MIN_VALUE / -1 traps).
# StrictArithmeticTransformer replaces division/remainder by a call to StrictArithmetic.{i,l}{div,rem}
# unless the divisor is a constant other than 0 / -1. Applied (a) to user programs when strictMode is on
# (Compiler.generateWebAssembly) and (b) to javac's ConstFold inside compiler.wasm (Patches), where
# javac folds '10 / 0' and relies on catch (ArithmeticException): before this, any program containing a
# constant division by zero crashed the compiler and wedged the playground. StrictArithmetic ships in
# runtime-classlib-teavm.bin but not in the SDK, so user code cannot see it.
#
# Applies to: github.com/konsoletyper/teavm-javac 2ddcf02e (master, 2026-09-04)

